  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve for $x\\in[-2\\pi,2\\pi]$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{5\\pi}{3},-\\frac{4\\pi}{3},\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$.",
          "worked": "Sine is positive in quadrants I and II.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{\\pi}{3}+2k\\pi\\\\\\text{or }x&=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}+2k\\pi.\\end{align*}$$\nFor each branch, $k=-1,0$ gives the values in the domain:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=-\\frac{5\\pi}{3},-\\frac{4\\pi}{3},\\frac{\\pi}{3},\\frac{2\\pi}{3}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\pm\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\pm\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$.",
          "worked": "Cosine is negative in quadrants II and III.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{3\\pi}{4}+2k\\pi\\\\\\text{or }x&=\\frac{5\\pi}{4}+2k\\pi.\\end{align*}$$\nFor each branch, $k=-1,0$ gives:\n$$x=\\pm\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\pm\\frac{5\\pi}{4}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan x=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{7\\pi}{4},-\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$.",
          "worked": "Tangent has reference angle $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ and period $\\pi$.\n$$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}+k\\pi.$$\nTaking $k=-2,-1,0,1$ gives:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=-\\frac{7\\pi}{4},-\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac{7\\pi}{6},-\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5\\pi}{6},\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$.",
          "worked": "Tangent has period $\\pi$ and $\\tan(-\\frac{\\pi}{6})=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$.\n$$x=-\\frac{\\pi}{6}+k\\pi.$$\nTaking $k=-1,0,1,2$ gives:\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=-\\frac{7\\pi}{6},-\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5\\pi}{6},\\frac{11\\pi}{6}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
